{"edges":[],"nodes":[{"area":null,"id":"scope:Combinatorics/tilings-board-placements/aztec-dragon-tilings","kind":"scope","lean":null,"status":"can_prove","summary":null,"title":"Aztec dragon tilings"},{"area":null,"id":"scope:Combinatorics/tilings-board-placements/domino-tilings-and-fibonacci-pell-products","kind":"scope","lean":null,"status":"fully_proved","summary":null,"title":"Domino tilings and Fibonacci–Pell products"},{"area":null,"id":"Combinatorics/tilings-board-placements/domino-tilings-l-grid-via-fibonacci","kind":"node","lean":"MetaMathlibExt.domino_tilings_L_grid_via_fibonacci","status":"can_prove","summary":"Let $f_n$ be the Fibonacci numbers, with $f_0 = 0$ and $f_1 = 1$. For natural numbers $n, m$ put $L_{n,m} = f_{n+1} f_m + f_n f_{m+1}$ and $a_n = f_{n+1} f_{n-1} + f_n^2$, where $n - 1$ is truncated subtraction. Then $L_{n,m} = f_{n+1} f_m + f_n f_{m+1}$ for all $n, m \\ge 1$, $L_{n,n-1} = a_n$ for all $n \\ge 2$, and $L_{n,n-1}^2 = L_{n,n} L_{n-1,n-1} + 1$ for all $n \\ge 2$.","title":"Tauraso's Cassini-type identity"},{"area":null,"id":"scope:Combinatorics/tilings-board-placements/fault-free-tilings-of-3-n-rectangles","kind":"scope","lean":null,"status":"fully_proved","summary":null,"title":"Fault-free tilings of 3 × n rectangles"},{"area":null,"id":"scope:Combinatorics/tilings-board-placements/fence-tilings-and-bi-periodic-fibonacci-numbers","kind":"scope","lean":null,"status":"can_prove","summary":null,"title":"Fence tilings and bi-periodic Fibonacci numbers"},{"area":null,"id":"scope:Combinatorics/tilings-board-placements/fixed-polycubes","kind":"scope","lean":null,"status":"fully_proved","summary":null,"title":"Fixed polycubes"},{"area":null,"id":"scope:Combinatorics/tilings-board-placements/lozenge-tilings-of-hexagons","kind":"scope","lean":null,"status":"can_prove","summary":null,"title":"Lozenge tilings of hexagons"},{"area":null,"id":"scope:Combinatorics/tilings-board-placements/nonattacking-bishops-and-anassas","kind":"scope","lean":nul